  "summary": "Brake pedal and master cylinder (main cylinder) installation: the master cylinder bolts to the engine side of the brake pedal housing/firewall with two nuts over a gasket; the pushrod passes through a boot and threads into a clevis pinned to the pedal arm with a clevis pin, wave washer and push-on retainer. The pedal pivots on bushings in the pedal housing with a return spring hooked on the housing bracket; the pedal pad cover and stainless trim plate are held by bent tabs.",
